.TH ZZ9K-TEST 1 "1 November 2026" "libzz9k"
.SH NAME
zz9k-test \- check libzz9k and the ZZ9000-family boards on this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/amix/bin/zz9k-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zz9k-test
lists the boards
.BR libzz9k (3)
finds behind
.B /dev/zz9ksvc0
and
.B /dev/zz9ksvc1
(the unit, the ABI version, the firmware version, the capability bits and the
CODEC service's flags), then decompresses a raw deflate, a zlib and a gzip
stream of test data in software and, where a board offers it, on the board,
and checks each result against the original and the two against each other.
A machine without a board passes with software only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every check holds, 1 otherwise.
.SH FILES
.B /opt/amix/lib/libzz9k.a
(linked in)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libzz9k (3),
.BR zz9ksvc (7)
